<title>NETHERLANDS: Renault boss to join Philips board.</title>
<headline>Renault boss to join Philips board.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of French carmaker Renault, Louis Schweitzer, will be proposed on March 21 as a member of the supervisory board of Philips Electronics NV, Philips said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Schweitzer, 54, also sits on the boards of aluminium and packaging company Pechiney, Bank Nationale de Paris, pharmaceuticals concern Roussel-Uclaf and bank Credit National.</p>
<p>Philips, one of the world's largest electronics companies, last week reported a 1996 net loss of 590 million guilders ($312 million).</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
